         "step": 1,
         "text": "The integrand is a product of x and an exponential, and the derivative of the exponent, \\( 2 \\), does not account for the factor x, so substitution does not apply and the product calls for integration by parts.",
         "rule_named": "technique selected by structure"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Take \\( u = 6 x \\) and \\( dv = e^{2 x}\\,dx \\), so \\( du = 6\\,dx \\) and \\( v = \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2} \\). Then the integral is \\( 3 x e^{2 x} - \\int 3 e^{2 x}\\,dx \\).",
         "rule_named": "integration by parts"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
